Video Player (com.palm.app.videoplayer 1.0.0): webOS Community Edition's player under Palm's
id, as webOS CE puts it on a TouchPad, and as the reference TouchPad (webOS CE 3.1.0) runs it.

webOS CE replaced Palm's Mojo 2 Video Player with an Enyo player of its own (the Videos app,
com.palm.app.videos 3.2.0, in the webOS Community Edition project, apps/com.palm.app.videos):
VideoEngine.js, a serialized seek and load gate over <video>, and PlayerApp.js, the card.
Videos' package script installs the same player under this id, so that apps that launch the
video player by name get it: index.html, depends.js, source/, css/, the four images in images/
and this appinfo.json (build/full-ce/videos-app/videoplayer-app/appinfo.json). Those files are
here as that script installs them, from the project's tree at bc1b6c5 ("Videos: localizable
strings"); like that script, its resources/ are not copied, so the player's text is English.
The player is webOS Archive's work, written for webOS CE (codepoet, 2026-11-15: "in CE we built
a new video player that replaces Palm's").

icon.png and icon-256x256.png are Palm's, from the original Video Player, which webOS CE left
in place: copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard, never released under an open licence, and
distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo, the Prelude fonts and the TouchPad wallpapers.

Until 2026-11-15 this folder held Palm's original Mojo 2 Video Player 1.0.0, which opened on a
phone-sized library screen the TouchPad never shows. Lunacy routes videos as before: only a
launch of this id, or a video file opened through the system's handler table, comes here;
CE's Videos (com.palm.app.videos) still goes to Android's player (card/WebosLinks.kt). Any
change Lunacy needs in the player is made in the webOS CE project and comes here with its next
release (rule 5 in CLAUDE.md).
